{"title":"1989 OIM Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the longitudes of the sides of a triangle.  Prove:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815e94b144f496e813104e2bf97099d86c48b775.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a-b}{a+b}+\\frac{b-c}{b+c}+\\frac{c-a}{c+a}&lt;\\frac{1}{16}\\]\" width=\"216\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, perform the Ravi Substitution; let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/e/cee0f6f7096ff929f675fa85b0ef11141e6bbafc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=x+y,b=y+z,c=z+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"239\" height=\"16\" /> for positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />. Then the inequality becomes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be099b22013513109cb4c07ab3507993ec51680.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff\\frac{x-z}{x+2y+z}+\\frac{y-x}{x+y+2z}+\\frac{z-y}{2x+y+z}&lt;\\frac{1}{16}\\]\" width=\"392\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62fcaedf7d6d58ad8e7176d455f67a2bb0954e84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff\\frac{2x+2y}{x+2y+z}-1+\\frac{2y+2z}{x+y+2z}-1+\\frac{2z+2x}{2x+y+z}-1&lt;\\frac{1}{16}\\]\" width=\"485\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbc1acb86e8a41fe195edaf772b2a5268a7f2781.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff\\frac{x+y}{x+2y+z}+\\frac{y+z}{x+y+2z}+\\frac{z+x}{2x+y+z}&lt;\\frac{49}{32}\\]\" width=\"392\" height=\"40\" />\nNext, since the inequality is homogenized, assume without loss of generality that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />; then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2ce64324029470d51db5c253f2dabc92a4dda63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff\\frac{1-z}{y+1}+\\frac{1-x}{z+1}+\\frac{1-y}{x+1}&lt;\\frac{49}{32}\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"40\" />\nInstead of proving the above, we prove a stronger inequality:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac698e4bee38f1bbd8a62b0a86fdd9f32f7de36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1-z}{y+1}+\\frac{1-x}{z+1}+\\frac{1-y}{x+1}\\le\\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"40\" />\nMultiplying out both sides:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/6682b52a7ef082a5bf8cc5c68b7cac9676ef3481.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff(1-z)(z+1)(x+1)+(1-x)(x+1)(y+1)+(1-y)(y+1)(z+1)\\le\\frac{3}{2}(x+1)(y+1)(z+1)\\]\" width=\"671\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff0418fac3a4544adeedc58c9de3fa4dc472ca57.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff(1-z^2)(x+1)+(1-x^2)(y+1)+(1-y^2)(z+1)\\le\\frac{3}{2}(xyz+xy+yz+zx+(x+y+z)+1)\\]\" width=\"664\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a29641c3f264c4617a8833a15cdb2b6a0932358d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff3+(x+y+z)-(x^2+y^2+z^2)-(x^2y+y^2z+z^2x)\\le\\frac{3}{2}(xyz+xy+yz+zx+2)\\]\" width=\"586\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5460f93af4c4b73ec0c7a3824195e11ef848fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff8-2(x^2+y^2+z^2)-2(x^2y+y^2z+z^2x)\\le3xyz+3(xy+yz+zx)+6\\]\" width=\"533\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf96d8c0e2424eeae7e78d70f0ec5767025b5633.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff3xyz+3(xy+yz+zx)+2(x^2+y^2+z^2)+2(x^2y+y^2z+z^2x)\\ge 2\\]\" width=\"533\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf6a48e7a8990bc9ea4075a469f096ef566895e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff3xyz+2(x+y+z)^2-(xy+yz+zx)+2(x^2y+y^2z+z^2x)\\ge 2\\]\" width=\"533\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/9292734f6f5d594edfab63adb7af246ae68c859e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff3xyz-(xy+yz+zx)+2(x^2y+y^2z+z^2x)\\ge 0\\]\" width=\"423\" height=\"20\" />\nNext, assume without loss of generality that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2d10458d60b6c47db0dd6f9abc1f1a4f80bf1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge y\\ge z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e700367a95bfe90bd317a354e88b030db2a294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\le x&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />. The upper bound is obvious (recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive), so we show the lower bound. Assume for the sake of contradiction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b559e9d02243978e7ef47a8febf52551851410e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />; then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a8677db0b724b33ec141fc29ccca9d107bf782a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x+y+z\\le x+x+x=3x&lt;3\\cdot\\frac{1}{3}=1\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"37\" />\nimplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab4da9d5e6f1e6a214ba0d9ccad88d7079c9272d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />, a contradiction, so the bounds hold. Then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d591351915995752480a2782df1b6789c354348.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff3xyz-(x(y+z)+yz)+2(x^2y+y^2z+z^2x)\\ge 0\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13cc895d6c0230f75f765b184afd417c7abbf465.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff yz(3x-1)-x(1-x)+2(x^2y+y^2z+z^2x)\\ge 0\\]\" width=\"418\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/5349ceea17d792d242c852a7d89eaf102ddfb9db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff yz(3x-1)+2(x^2y+y^2z+z^2x)\\ge x(1-x)\\]\" width=\"385\" height=\"20\" />\nDue to the bounds, the left-hand side is nonnegative, but the right-hand side is nonpositive, so we are done.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe4.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe4.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181659\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 158/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5934/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26058:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017181659 and revision id 246991. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}